node_modules/
dist/
# pnpm's content-addressed package cache, when it is configured to live in the
# repo rather than under ~/.local/share/pnpm. Hundreds of megabytes of upstream
# tarballs, rebuildable by `pnpm install` — and untracked-but-unignored it is
# one `git add -A` away from being committed.
.pnpm-store/
.env
.env.*
# The committed shape of a .env. Carries no values, only names and comments.
!.env.example
# Refills the .env files from ~/.nns. Operator-local: it encodes one machine's
# layout of the secret store, so sharing it shares nothing useful and invites
# somebody to run it against a store that is not theirs. Untracked 2026-08-15;
# earlier revisions stay in history if it is ever needed back.
scripts/restore-env.sh
*.log
.DS_Store

# An operator's live delegate data (labels.example.json is the template).
packages/delegate/labels.json
deploy/delegate/labels/
deploy/collaborator/labels/
# Agreed referral partner rates: box-local, never published.
deploy/settlement/private/

# Copied from @nimiqnames/resolver at build time (packages/app/scripts/copy-resolver-bundle.mjs).
packages/app/public/nns.js

# ── Working notes, kept out of the published tree ───────────────────────────
# These exist in the maintainer's checkout and are deliberately not part of the
# repository: they are the internal working record, not the product. They name
# hosts, describe unfinished mitigations and argue about rules that the spec
# now states — material that helps nobody build against NNS and helps somebody
# else find its soft edges. The spec (`docs/nns-spec-v1.md`) is the authority;
# `docs/integration.md` is how to build on it.
MAP.md
/docs/decisions.md
/docs/status.md
/docs/history/
/docs/audit/
/docs/runbooks/deploy.md
/docs/runbooks/testing.md
/tasks/
